// SEVENTEEN generated_conformance_floor ROWS LEFT THIS ROSTER BECAUSE THE FIX THIS BRANCH CARRIES
// MADE THEM PASS — THIS ROSTER'S OWN REMOVAL PATH, NOT A ROSTER EDIT. They were among the
// identities the required floor reported as KNOWN-RED-RUNTIME-ERRORED — enrolled as expected-red
// but throwing rather than failing, so producing no verdict — and every one threw for the reason
// this branch repairs: the reference-closure collector narrowed on binding metadata its own
// producer never populates, so a genuinely declared name resolved to nothing and the call threw
// `no such function`.
//
// With the closure derived from lexical binders instead, the calls resolve and the witnesses
// answer PASS, so the floor reported them STALE-QUARANTINE — which IS gating (claim_executor
// `required_floor_outcome_is_clean` lists seven causes and includes it), unlike the
// runtime-errored arm, which is reported and deliberately NOT gating. The fix moved rows from a
// non-gating arm into a gating one, and this removal is the remedy the floor's own message names.
//
// THE POPULATION IS 82, NOT THE SEVENTEEN AN EARLIER REVISION NAMED, recorded rather than silently
// swapped because the two numbers are two measurements of one fact and the stale one was
// load-bearing. Seventeen was measured before this branch carried main, against a roster that no
// longer exists. Run 32670979986 reports `stale_quarantine=82`, and all 82 are removed here.
//
// THE FOUR generated_coproduct_exhaustiveness_* ROWS ARE PART OF THAT 82 AND ARE REMOVED WITH IT.
// An earlier revision retained them as the discriminating half of the edit, because they sat in
// the same generated module and were NOT reported passing. True of that measurement, false of
// this one: the same run names all four as STALE-QUARANTINE. Retaining them would enrol four rows
// this branch makes pass — the gating failure the removal exists to avoid — so the retention is
// withdrawn, and with it the claim that this edit carries a same-module discriminating half.
//
// SUPERSEDED BY THE MERGE THAT CARRIES THIS BLOCK; kept because it records a measurement (run
// 32670979986, stale_quarantine=82) nothing else carries. Measured at this merge: main's roster is
// a strict SUBSET of this branch's — every identity this branch removed is already absent from
// main, which removed 127 against this branch's 99 — so the merged roster is main's 65 and THIS
// BRANCH NO LONGER PERFORMS A REMOVAL. Resolved by set algebra, not by choosing a side: base 192,
// ours 93, theirs 65, additions on neither side, and `comm -13 ours theirs` is empty, which
// establishes the subset and that taking main's rows loses nothing this branch had removed.
//
// ONE QUESTION LEFT OPEN, because asserting either way would be invention: the 82 left because
// THIS branch's fix made them pass, and main removed them without that fix. Either they pass for
// an independent reason, or main's larger removal has a different warrant; both are consistent
// with what is measured and nothing in this merge distinguishes them. The floor run on the merged
// head decides it — if any of the 82 re-appears as a fresh red, this note is where to start.

fn floor_expected_red_chunk_07() -> List<String> {
  Empty {}
}

fn floor_expected_red_chunk_08() -> List<String> {
   Cons { head: "v2.test.execution.dag_add_emit_round_trip.dag_add_domain_coerce_accepts_holds", tail: Cons { head: "v2.test.execution.dag_add_emit_round_trip.dag_add_domain_translate_accepts_holds", tail: Empty {} } }
