// RETIRED chunk_23 EXPECTED-RED ADMISSION history. PositionGenericTypeArgument now constructs the
// missing element obligation at the direct-call seam; the witness remains enrolled as an ordinary
// permanent regression control, tightened to require DeclaredTypeNotInhabited at the generic type
// argument position, while only its temporary expected-red admission is deleted here.
//
// THE MEASUREMENT IS CARRIED HERE RATHER THAN CITED: a row that has told an assertion not to
// assert is where a reader most needs the reason, and a pointer to a pull request is worthless if
// that request has not landed (or never does). The four facts, standalone:
//
//   1. WHAT THE WITNESS ASSERTS. `FreeMonoid<Node>` passed to a parameter declared
//      `FreeMonoid<NormalizedTree>` -- a container-element type mismatch at a direct call
//      argument -- must be REFUSED. The witness holds `!compile_dag_rust_emit_check(...)`, so it
//      passes only when the embedded fixture fails to compile.
//   2. IT IS ACCEPTED, AND THE CONTROLS ESTABLISH IT. Two fixtures carrying the IDENTICAL
//      container-element mismatch, built from a locally declared record with no `Node`, no
//      `v2.std.node` and no occurrence identity anywhere -- one reusing the wrapper name
//      `NormalizedTree`, one using a corpus-unique wrapper name -- BOTH COMPILE CLEAN ON MAIN
//      (@ ddb7f533e4e), zero blocking diagnostics. They share nothing with the occurrence-identity
//      cut, so the acceptance is a property of the compiler, not of this branch.
//   3. THE PREVIOUS GREEN WAS NOT ITS OWN ASSERTION. On main the real fixture refuses with exactly
//      `UnresolvedType std.occurrence_identity.OccurrenceId` x2 and `ScopedOccurrenceRef` x1, and
//      carries NO type-mismatch diagnostic. `v2.std.node` referenced those two types fully
//      qualified WITHOUT importing that module, so every closure importing `v2.std.node` inherited
//      them. This branch adds the import, they resolve, and the accidental refusal goes with them.
//   4. DISCHARGED NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER. A child obligation constructed at
//      PositionGenericTypeArgument and decided by declared_type_inhabitance. This trigger is
//      discharged by direct_call_generic_type_argument_inhabitance_diags constructing that exact
//      obligation and handing it to declared_type_obligation_diags. The earlier trigger,
//      `container_element_nominal_brand_mismatch` reaching the direct-call-argument position, was
//      already satisfied while this mismatch remained accepted: direct_call_arg_type_mismatch
//      already called it here. It named a route rather than the missing capability and could have
//      retired this row while the wall was still dead.
//
// Measured with the witness's own oracle (`compile_dag_rust_emit_check`) alongside
// `compile_dag_diagnostic_census`, over both corpora, 2026-08-27.
//
// Every other row here names a witness that FAILS and that someone is repairing. This one names a
// witness whose SUBJECT was never guarded, and the repair it waits on is a compiler wall that does
// not exist yet, not a witness repair. The header's rule (a row belongs here only while someone
// is fixing it) exists so this roster cannot become a skip list; this row is admitted against its
// letter with the tension named: it has a trigger, it is at identity grain, and it is on the same
// self-emptying path as everything else -- the moment the wall lands, the witness passes, this
// roster reds the build naming this row, and the row is deleted. What it does NOT have is an owner
// mid-repair today.
//
// THE CLASS IS RUNG INFLATION, DESIGN 4b(1) -- NOT a 4b(3) rung drop, and the distinction decides
// what a reader may do with this row. Nothing regressed. The container-element mismatch judgment
// at a direct call argument does not fire and never did:
// `record_literal_container_element_mismatch_at_call_arg_still_refuses` was GREEN ON MAIN because
// `v2.std.node` referenced `std.occurrence_identity.OccurrenceId` and `ScopedOccurrenceRef` fully
// qualified WITHOUT importing that module, so every closure importing `v2.std.node` inherited two
// `UnresolvedType` diagnostics and refused for THAT reason. Measured on main @ ddb7f533e4e with the
// witness's own oracle, the fixture's refusal is exactly those two diagnostics with no
// type-mismatch diagnostic; the same mismatch built from a locally declared record, with no `Node`
// and no `v2.std.node`, COMPILES CLEAN ON MAIN. This branch adds the import that resolves them,
// and the accidental refusal goes with them.
//
// SO THE ROW A READER MUST NOT WRITE is "restore the previous behaviour". It was an accident, and
// re-adding unresolved references to buy back the red would manufacture a refusal from a defect --
// what this roster exists to make visible, not to launder.
//
// A witness green on a defect in its own closure is NEGATIVE coverage, not weak coverage: it is
// cited as evidence the wall is live, so the class never ranks for climbing. The nominal sibling
// `record_literal_nominal_mismatch_at_call_arg_still_refuses` stays green through a DIFFERENT path
// (`literal_introduction_type_mismatch`, whose actual is a record literal rather than a call),
// which is why the family read as coherent and was not.
//
// The class row and its ceiling are ALSO filed in
// `docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md` (gunbc#9457, against main, because the
// finding is about main) -- in ADDITION to the four facts above, never instead, because merge
// order is not this branch's to control and that row may land after this one or not at all.
// THE ENROLMENT COULD NOT LAND THERE, mechanically: on main this witness still PASSES,
// `required_floor_outcome_is_clean` requires `stale_quarantine` to be empty, and an enrolled row
// that passes reds the build -- so enrolling it on main would red main's own required floor. It
// fails here, the only tree where it is honestly enrollable.
//
// REMOVAL TRIGGER, CORRECTED AND NOW FIRED: a child obligation constructed at
// PositionGenericTypeArgument and decided by declared_type_inhabitance. The witness is the
// permanent regression control for that capability.
// The interpreter realizes terminal `first` as a raw element or Null while emitted Rust realizes
// the same modeled operation as Optional<T>. This exact specimen executes and returns false. It
// stays enrolled after repair: when it becomes true this roster row is deleted and the claim
// remains as the regression control.
fn floor_expected_red_chunk_interpreter_first_optional_divergence() -> List<String> {
  Cons { head: "test.claim.cli_dispatch_surface.interpreter_first_returns_the_modeled_optional", tail: Empty {} }
}

// THIRTEEN FURTHER IDENTITIES RETIRED 2026-08-26 BY ONE REPAIR, and the number is the finding. The
// local-binding-shadow repair -- a call site spelling a name held by both a local binding and a
// module-level free function now reaches the LOCAL -- was enrolled with ONE row of its own. On the
// first required run after it landed, thirteen OTHER enrolled reds across five unrelated modules
// passed: test.claim.host_phase_status (2), test.claim.interpreter_replacement_cut_witness_test
// (2), test.claim.srv3_subsumption (6), v2.test.claim.staging (2) and
// v2.test.emit.produced_decl_support_preserved (1). None was authored as a shadow probe or names
// the class; they were filed as ordinary reds against their own subjects, which is exactly what a
// SILENT wrong value looks like from the consumer's side -- the fold returns a plausible answer,
// the assertion disagrees, and the row gets written against the assertion. This list was carrying
// thirteen symptoms of one cause, legible from none of them.
//
// THE ROWS ARE REMOVED AND THE WITNESSES ARE NOT (DESIGN 4b(4)). Every one stays enrolled and now
// passes, which keeps the repair's reach measured rather than asserted: if the gate regresses,
// thirteen independent modules go red before the shadow fixture does.

// THE LIVE-TREE-ADMISSION CHUNK -- THE OTHER HALF OF gunbc#9106, a completion rather than a new
// admission.
//
// IT IS NOT NUMBERED, BECAUSE OF A DEFECT THAT WAS ABOUT TO LAND, NOT A STYLE PREFERENCE. Three
// open branches each mint a `floor_expected_red_chunk_24` into this file: gunbc#9591 (this one),
// gunbc#9587 (one add-slice row) and gunbc#9569 (six
// `sole_constructor_completeness_audit_probe_test` rows, also six of the 47 below). The numeric
// suffix is a SHARED MUTABLE COUNTER whose next value every concurrent lane computes independently
// from the same base, so collision under concurrency is the expected outcome, not a risk.
//
// WHAT MAKES IT WORSE THAN AN ORDINARY CONFLICT, and why a distinct name is the construction rather
// than the courtesy: two lanes appending a same-named `fn` at DIFFERENT offsets can merge with NO
// CONFLICT MARKERS, leaving one file with two definitions of one name. This repository has
// measured what happens next -- `test.claim.duplicate_definition_binding_probe_test` exists
// because a duplicate definition is SILENTLY ACCEPTED and the later binding wins -- so the merge
// would not fail; it would quietly drop one lane's rows and stay green. A position-derived name is
// a second naming scheme for something the declaration already names (DESIGN section 3), and this
// is that rule's cost arriving in the merge graph.
//
// So the chunk is named for WHAT IT ADMITS. A meaning-carrying name cannot be independently
// derived by two lanes, making the collision unrepresentable instead of detected.
//
// #9106 deleted the floor's stale live-tree decline -- a FILE-GRAIN PREDICTION that a witness
// reading the live tree could not participate in the hermetic fold, which had stopped agreeing
// with what the interpreter does. Deleting it was correct and admitted a population that had never
// executed: on main run 33145062452 (3a8344b5c3) the floor reports failed=47, and these are those
// 47.
//
// WHY THEY BELONG HERE, the question this roster's header says to ask before enrolling anything.
// Every one EXECUTES AND ANSWERS FALSE -- the run classifies each as `FAIL ... returned
// Bool(false)`, the semantic verdict this roster is defined over. None route-gaps (no overlap with
// `v2.workflow.floor_route_gap`), none produces a non-verdict, and none is a budget outcome.
//
// AN EARLIER REVISION OF THAT SENTENCE ALSO CLAIMED EACH ROW "REACHES ITS SUBJECT", AND THE RUN
// DOES NOT ESTABLISH THAT. `Bool` has no spelling for "I could not observe my subject", so an
// unreached subject and a genuine NO render identically as `returned Bool(false)`. Execution is
// established; subject-reachability is not -- exactly the class this document names as
// execution-provenance loss. The clause is removed rather than softened, because a reader quoting
// it would be quoting a property nothing measured. The live candidate is named in the follow-ups
// below.
// That last exclusion is load-bearing and is why this chunk closes two of the run's four causes
// rather than all four. The same run reports 44 `interrupted_before_verdict` and 2
// `completed_over_cost_requirement`, and NONE of them is here.
//
// WHY NOT, as a refusal rather than a scope note: an interrupted row produced NO VERDICT.
// Enrolling it would assert "runs and fails, and someone is fixing it" about an identity that
// never answered -- precisely the 101-row mistake this file's header opens with -- and
// `ExpectedRedArm` refuses budget outcomes by construction, so the enrolment would not even take.
// The 2 completed-over-cost rows answered, but what they owe is a COST, not a failure; enrolling
// them would assert an expected FAILURE they do not exhibit. Cost is not a verdict, and the
// verdict roster cannot carry it.
//
// THE POPULATION IS BOUNDED AND MEASURED, at identity grain, on the run named above: 44
// interrupted, all on the CPU clock against `required_floor_claim_cpu_safety_limit_ms`'s 5000ms,
// concentrated in live-tree corpus witnesses (13 in
// `v2.test.claim.enforcement.grammar_coverage_witness`, 6 in
// `v2.test.claim.enforcement_live_witness`, 6 in
// `v2.test.claim.complexity.accumulator_copy_roster_gate`, the rest spread across 10 modules);
// and 2 completed-over-cost, both in `test.claim.transport_script_wall_compile_red`, on the wall
// clock at 18882ms and 19024ms against 10000ms. Every interrupted figure is a LOWER BOUND -- the
// deadline preempted the measurement -- so their real cost is unmeasured and the sum is not this
// population's cost.
//
// WHERE THEY GO, AND IT IS NOT A NEW MECHANISM. `v2.workflow.required_floor` states the remedies
// exhaustively -- reduce what the witness reaches for, or enrol it in a lane declaring its own
// dated ceiling -- and names relocation as forbidden. A carrier for exactly this axis is built and
// open as gunbc#9517 (`v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt`, joined by a `DeclinedCostDebt` arm in
// `required_floor`). These 46 identities were handed to that lane at identity grain with clock,
// figure and limit per row, rather than duplicated here: authoring them into a module not on main
// would fork the authority this chunk exists to respect.
//
// AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS PARAGRAPH ASSERTED THAT #9517's ROSTER RETURNS `Empty`, AS A
// FIRST-HAND READING. The reading was honest -- `floor_cost_debt_chunks()` on
// `origin/session/witty-wren-148` was `Empty {}` when taken -- and WRONG WITHIN THE HOUR, because
// the branch was moving while I read it. That is this document's own transcribed-measurement
// class on the shortest possible clock: a bare present-tense claim about ANOTHER LANE'S HEAD has
// no producer on this side of the boundary that could re-derive it, so nothing here refuses when
// it goes false. The sentence is deleted rather than re-pinned, because a second number would rot
// the same way.
//
// WHAT IS KNOWN AND WHAT IS NOT, kept separate: that lane reports the 46 enrolled as a
// separately-labelled cost population, explicitly NOT claimed to pass, keyed on MARGINAL cpu so
// that draining a row displaces no shared fill onto its successor. That is their measurement,
// reported to this lane and not re-derived by it. What THIS module can stand behind is its own
// side only: these 46 are absent from this roster, deliberately, for the reason stated above.
//
// RUNG, DECLARED HONESTLY (DESIGN 4b(3)): on MAIN the cost axis stays BELOW the floor's own bar --
// the run still stops on it, so nothing is silently admitted, but 46 identities reach no usable
// verdict every run and no mechanism ON MAIN holds them. Bounded, identity-grain, re-measurable.
// RESTORATION TRIGGER: a roster ON MAIN carries these 46 under an O=R admission, at which point
// they are counted debt on the cost axis instead of an ungoverned cause. The trigger names the
// CAPABILITY and deliberately not an artifact (DESIGN 4b(3), 2026-08-26): NOT "#9517 merges",
// because a merge of an empty roster closes none of them, and NOT "that lane enrols them",
// because an enrolment on an unmerged branch changes nothing about what the required run on main
// observes.
//
// THE TREE ALREADY DEMANDED THIS, AND THE RUN CONFIRMED IT BY EXECUTION.
//
// The prediction was registered before the run: enrolling
// `legacy_test_behavior_unclassified_frontier_is_zero` would satisfy the assertion the
// `quarantine_probe_disposition_witness_test` claims make ABOUT this roster, so they would stop
// failing and report STALE-QUARANTINE. Run 33154432928 answered `failed=0 stale_quarantine=3`,
// naming exactly those three, and they are removed here -- by the roster's own removal path, the
// mechanism working rather than an edit correcting a mistake.
//
// THE PREDICTION SAID FOUR AND THE ANSWER WAS THREE, recorded because the error is the more
// instructive half. The fourth name was `legacy_test_behavior_unclassified_frontier_is_zero`
// itself, and it did NOT flip -- correctly. It is the row the join is ABOUT, not a row that passes
// as a consequence: it still fails on its own subject, and this roster still holds it. Conflating
// "the identity a witness names" with "an identity that changes state when the witness is
// satisfied" produced the extra row, and a join has both roles in it at once.
//
// WHY THE ENROLMENT WAS STILL RIGHT FOR ALL THREE. They failed on main and answer false, so they
// met this roster's admission when added; what removed them is that the same change repaired
// their subject. A roster that could not hold a row for one run and release it on the next would
// force the author to predict the repair perfectly before landing it.
// `test.claim.quarantine_probe_disposition_witness_test.the_former_live_tree_declined_row_is_now_expected_red`
// asserts that `test.claim.legacy_test_behavior_disposition_acceptance_test.legacy_test_behavior_unclassified_frontier_is_zero`
// is held by this roster -- authored against the post-#9106 world and failing since, because the
// row it names was never added. That witness is itself one of the 47. So four of these rows (the
// three `quarantine_probe_disposition_witness_test` claims and the `legacy_test_behavior` one they
// join against) are expected to leave this chunk on the first run after it lands, by this
// roster's own removal path rather than by an edit.
//
// THE 47 ARE NOT ONE CAUSE, AND THREE GROUPS INSIDE THEM CARRY A REMEDY THIS ROSTER CANNOT STATE.
// A row here is a bare identity string with no reason field, so enrolment says exactly one thing
// -- expected to fail -- about rows that fail for at least six distinct causes with different
// remedies. That is a limit of the mechanism, not of this chunk, and the three groups are named so
// the next reader does not conclude one cause. All three are FOLLOW-UPS rather than reasons to
// withhold enrolment, because enrolment is a REVERSIBLE HOLDING STATE WITH A LOUD EXIT: the floor
// refuses on an enrolled row that starts passing and names it -- the same path by which this
// change removes one.
//
//   1. THE THREE `guarantee_floor_class_probe_witness` GENERIC-INSTANTIATION ROWS FAIL BECAUSE
//      A WALL LANDED, NOT BECAUSE THE HOLE IS OPEN. They assert a hole is still open; it is
//      not. The discriminating evidence: BOTH of that hole's controls PASS
//      (`floor_generic_instantiation_monomorphic_control_refuses`,
//      `floor_generic_instantiation_green_control_is_clean`) and the SIBLING hole probe
//      `floor_field_through_generics_is_still_silently_accepted` also passes -- so the harness
//      reached the judgment and the other hole is genuinely still open; a harness that saw
//      nothing would have taken the sibling down too. That module's own
//      `guarantee_floor_class_probe_scope_note` prescribes the remedy verbatim: such a probe
//      "flip[s] RED on the day the wall lands, which is the signal to rewrite the row as
//      `ExpectBlockingRefusal` rather than to delete the probe" -- DESIGN 4b(4)'s rule that a
//      greened expecting-red probe becomes a permanent regression control. Enrolment holds them
//      honestly (they do fail) while recording nothing about WHY, so the rewrite is owed and the
//      stale-quarantine arm will demand it.
//
//   2. THE FOUR `sole_constructor_completeness_audit_probe_test` f10 ROWS ANSWERED AN OPEN QUESTION
//      THE FIRST TIME THEY RAN. Their block annotation states a question rather than a marked
//      red -- "to test whether resolution of an unqualified bare-name construction depends on
//      import statement order" -- and the answer is YES: `_ab` fails while `_ba` passes on
//      identical source with the imports swapped, and the two direct probes fail in OPPOSITE
//      directions, both predicted by last-import-wins. That is the census-AMBIGUOUS resolution
//      hole DESIGN 4b already records as decidable once scoped. The distinction is decidable in
//      the file: f13 and f19, enrolled here on the same footing, carry an explicit "Deliberately
//      RED" marking and the f10 four do not.
//
//   3. THE THREE `cost_coverage_witness` ROWS ARE THE SUBJECT-REACHABILITY CANDIDATE. That
//      module has 10 test fns; the 7 that pass survive an empty subject (one reads
//      `(receipt.files_attempted == 0) || ...`) and the 3 that fail demand non-zero content.
//      Consistent with a genuine NO and equally with a subject never reached, and no run
//      distinguishes them. Enrolled as failing, which is what was observed; NOT asserted to be
//      semantic.
//
// The classification, controls and per-row execution behind all three are crisp-newt-899's
// triage, verified here against the cited files rather than accepted on report.
//
// ONE STALE PREMISE FOUND WHILE CHECKING THE ABOVE, load-bearing for a carrier this chunk
// overlaps. `gunbc.declined_live_tree_defect_classification` states that it "is not an
// expected-red enrolment and must never become one: enrolling a row here would assert that the
// floor runs it and that it fails, and the floor does not run it at all." Eight of the modules it
// classifies contain rows enrolled here, and the floor DOES now run them -- they are in run
// 33145062452's FAIL lines. So that clause's REASON has been overtaken by #9106; it is not wrong
// about authority substitution in general, but it is premised on a non-execution that no longer
// holds. Not edited here, because it is that carrier's to correct and a second account of one
// fact is the defect either way -- reported to its owner instead.
//
// WHAT THIS CHUNK IS NOT: a coverage claim or a disposition. Each row is a defect somebody owns,
// visible at identity grain, and the chunk can only shrink under an honest run -- a member that
// starts passing reds the build naming itself. Its length is the debt #9106 surfaced; the debt was
// always there, and now it is counted.
// ONE MEMBER OF THIS CHUNK HAS A PER-ROW MECHANISM, MEASURED BY EXECUTION, written here because
// the bulk enrolment establishes THAT the row fails and not WHY -- and for this row the why is
// what stops the next reader closing it the cheap way.
//
// `v2.test.execution.self_host_candidate_generation.candidate_generation_translate_self_emit_dag_add_slice_holds`
// runs `generate_translate_self_emit_candidate` -- `infer` composed with `translate` -- over the
// dag add slice and holds only on `Accepted`, with the emitted node equal to
// `dag_emitted_add_fn_node()` and no diagnostic carried.
//
// A RECEIPT, AND EXPLICITLY NOT AN INSTRUMENT -- stated because DESIGN's
// name-the-instrument-never-transcribe-its-output ruling reaches this paragraph, and half of it
// bites here. At main 3a8344b5c, a probe module returning each stage's verdict as a Symbol
// answered `infer_accepted` for `infer(dag_add_emitted_root)` and `infer_grounding_not_derived`
// for `generate_translate_self_emit_candidate` over that same root and `dag_add_target_model`.
// Infer ACCEPTS; the composition refuses.
//
// WHAT THE RULING DOES AND DOES NOT REACH HERE. Its subject is a live claim transcribed as a
// standing figure, which rots because the thing it describes moves. This one names a fixed tree,
// so it stays true of that tree forever -- the dated-receipt half the ruling preserves. What it
// DOES reach is reproducibility: the probe was a throwaway module and no `.dag` entry point
// re-derives this, so a reader cannot re-run it. That gap is this note's own next-rung trigger: a
// `.dag` entry returning the per-stage verdicts for one root would let this paragraph name a
// producer instead of a commit.
//
// IT IS NOT DELETED IN FAVOUR OF THE STRUCTURAL ACCOUNT BELOW, because that account cannot
// establish it. Reading the gate tells you translate CAN refuse an underived grounding; it cannot
// tell you that infer ACCEPTED this input rather than rejecting it earlier, and that fact locates
// the work in the derivation rules rather than in translate. A structural argument reaching the
// same conclusion without the observation would be the inference this repository keeps recording
// as a diagnostic name read as a mechanism.
//
// THE REFUSAL IS THE DECLARED FRONTIER, NOT A DEFECT IN EITHER STAGE. The fixture root is
// `TypeNode { connective: Arrow }` over `Conj` inhabitants, and `v2.compiler.infer`
// `node_grounding_frontier_note` states that v2 derives grounding for four of the closed
// vocabulary's twelve kinds (Branch, Match, Loop, and Transform in its add shape) and no other.
// So infer records `GroundingNotDerived`, and `translate_grounding_derived_gate_subtree` routes
// that variant through `canonical_grounding_from_inferred_facts` and refuses with the frontier's
// own typed reason. The gate does what it was built to do on a tree the frontier has not reached.
//
// AND NO REPAIR TO THE GATE ALONE WOULD GREEN THIS ROW, so the refusal must not be read as
// locating the work in translate: `inferred_facts_not_derived` returns the frontier diagnostic on
// infer's ACCEPTED path, so even an accepting translate leaves the witness's `d == None` conjunct
// false. Both conjuncts fail for the one cause.
//
// WHY THE CHEAP GREEN IS FORBIDDEN, the whole reason this note exists. The sibling witnesses in
// `v2.test.execution.dag_add_emit_round_trip` pass on the SAME fixture because they build their
// `InferredTree` from a hand-authored facts lookup answering `DerivedGrounding`. Making `infer`
// answer that way for connective nodes generally is precisely the `root == root` grounding
// `node_grounding_frontier_note` records as the defect the frontier carrier REPLACED -- every node
// typed as itself, read downstream as an established judgment. The honest repair is a derivation
// rule for the kinds this slice uses: v2 self-host lane work, not a witness edit.
//
// ITS REMOVAL TRIGGER IS NOT RESTATED HERE, DELIBERATELY: it is already modeled, with population
// and blocker, in `gunbc.guarantee_stall` `self_host_candidate_generation_add_slice_stall`.
// Copying those fields into a comment would fork that authority into prose that drifts on its own
// (DESIGN 2/3, and 4c's rule that an annotation must not restate what a declaration says), and no
// `Accepted` program can read a comment, so the copy could never be the thing that is checked.
// What this roster owns is the RELATION: this row is that stall's executing consumer, so when the
// stall's trigger is met the witness passes, stale quarantine reds the build naming the row, and
// the two delete together.
// TWO ARMS OF THE EXPECTED-TYPE PATH WITNESS, ENROLLED BECAUSE THE WALL THEY ASSERT DOES NOT HOLD
// ON THAT PATH AND WAS NOT BROKEN BY THE BRANCH THAT FOUND IT. Both assert that a generic
// application reaching a declared return it does not inhabit produces a blocking diagnostic. It
// does not. The specimen is not synthetic in origin: gunbc.runner_slot_allocation
// gunbc_runner_memory_per_core carried exactly that shape, typechecked, and yielded
// Measure { count: 3 } -- three BYTES per core -- which drove the entire fleet to
// deployment=refused cause=zero_runner_width under a diagnostic naming neither the ratio nor the
// missing conversion.
//
// CAUSATION IS SETTLED WITHOUT A MAIN CONTROL BUILD, and the argument is stated so a reader can
// check it rather than trust it: the branch enrolling these rows changes NO compiler source. Its
// entire diff against b60fc7dd61 under src/ is empty -- only dag/ corpus rows and this roster move
// -- so no edit on it can have opened a type judgment. The admission predates the fixture.
//
// AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS ROW ENROLLED ONE IDENTITY AND CARRIED A MEASURED TABLE THAT WAS NOT
// MEASURING ITS SUBJECT, and it is recorded here because the failure is instructive rather than
// clerical. That row read a Gibibyte against a declared ByteSize through a source importing
// std.measure, with the verdict filtered to the diagnostic class DeclaredTypeNotInhabited. Both
// halves were wrong. The census compiles a SYNTHETIC SINGLE-MODULE source, so corpus imports do not
// resolve -- a trivially VALID std.measure program produces 92 BLOCKING diagnostics -- and the
// class filter hid every one of them, which is the only reason the pair ever appeared to work. The
// old red refused because its imports did not resolve, and its own positive control refused for the
// identical reason while asserting admission. A class name is a fact about diagnostic QUALITY; only
// the refusal is the admission fact.
//
// THE REPLACEMENT SPECIMENS IMPORT NOTHING AND THE ORACLE COUNTS BLOCKING ROWS, and with that the
// matrix does not merely locate the defect -- it establishes that the defect is much larger than
// the row this file used to carry. Measured, all executed:
//
//   plain record vs plain record, different fields          ADMITTED  <- this row
//   generic argument at position zero, phantom parameter    ADMITTED  <- this row
//   generic argument at position zero, carried in a field   ADMITTED  <- this row
//   generic argument at the MIDDLE of three                 ADMITTED  <- this row
//   generic argument at the LAST of three                   ADMITTED  <- this row
//   different application HEAD, same argument               ADMITTED  <- this row
//   NESTED argument, at the middle position                 ADMITTED  <- this row
//   matching application, each of the three forms           admitted  (positive controls)
//   a PRIMITIVE where an application is declared            refused
//   a primitive call-result mismatch                        refused
//   a blatant primitive mismatch                            refused   (liveness)
//   a valid source                                          admitted  (opposite control)
//
// SO THE HONEST STATEMENT IS NOT ABOUT GENERICS. In declared-return position two NOMINAL types are
// not compared at all; refusal survives only where a PRIMITIVE is on one side. Every generic row is
// an instance of that, which is why the plain-record row is enrolled in its own right.
//
// AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS ROW CLAIMED THE CONSTRUCTOR HEAD WAS COMPARED and narrowed the defect
// to the type-argument vector on that basis. Its only evidence was a PRIMITIVE returned where an
// application was declared, which establishes nothing about comparing two applications. Two
// different heads are admitted. The claim was a guess wearing a measurement's clothes, and it is
// the same failure this file already records one paragraph above.
//
// SEVEN IDENTITIES, because each names a discrimination a partial repair could miss while greening
// the others -- and greening them is not harmless, since this roster SELF-EMPTIES on pass. A repair
// comparing only the first argument would retire the two position-zero rows while the production
// Measure<Memory, Gibi, Nat> hole, which differs at the MIDDLE argument, stayed open. One comparing
// heads and arguments pairwise could zip to the shorter vector and miss arity. One comparing only
// the outermost argument would miss nesting. One confined to applications would miss plain records.
// A single row could not tell any of those apart.
//
// DISSOLVE-ON: the declared-return expected-type comparison rejecting every enrolled mismatch --
// the plain-record pair by nominal identity, and the same-head same-arity applications at argument
// positions zero, one and two plus the enrolled nested argument-one case, together with the
// distinct-head pair. Stated as the positions and shapes actually enrolled rather than as "every
// argument recursively", because a trigger may not promise a generality no specimen exercises.
// This roster's
// self-emptying arm makes that event announce itself: when the wall arrives, this row PASSES,
// which reds the build and names itself for removal. The witness itself is permanent under
// DESIGN 4b(4) -- it flips to a regression control rather than retiring.
fn floor_expected_red_chunk_24() -> List<String> {
  Cons { head: "test.claim.declared_type_expected_type_path_witness.w_a_wrong_type_argument_at_a_declared_return_is_refused",
  tail: Cons { head: "test.claim.declared_type_expected_type_path_witness.w_a_wrong_type_argument_carried_in_a_field_is_refused",
  tail: Cons { head: "test.claim.declared_type_expected_type_path_witness.w_a_wrong_middle_type_argument_at_a_declared_return_is_refused",
  tail: Cons { head: "test.claim.declared_type_expected_type_path_witness.w_a_different_application_head_at_a_declared_return_is_refused",
  tail: Cons { head: "test.claim.declared_type_expected_type_path_witness.w_a_wrong_last_type_argument_at_a_declared_return_is_refused",
  tail: Cons { head: "test.claim.declared_type_expected_type_path_witness.w_a_wrong_nested_type_argument_at_a_declared_return_is_refused",
  tail: Cons { head: "test.claim.declared_type_expected_type_path_witness.w_a_different_plain_record_at_a_declared_return_is_refused", tail: Empty {} } } } } } } }
}

fn floor_expected_red_chunk_live_tree_admission() -> List<String> {
